:::

:::details 2. Bottom-up 2-D table
`dp[i][j]` = first `i` chars of `s1` and first `j` of `s2` can form the first `i + j` of `s3`. `dp[i][j] = (dp[i−1][j] and s1[i−1] == s3[i+j−1]) or (dp[i][j−1] and s2[j−1] == s3[i+j−1])`.

**Java**

```java
class Solution {
    public boolean isInterleave(String s1, String s2, String s3) {
        int n = s1.length(), m = s2.length();
        if (n + m != s3.length()) return false;
        boolean[][] dp = new boolean[n + 1][m + 1];
        dp[0][0] = true;
        for (int i = 0; i <= n; i++)
            for (int j = 0; j <= m; j++) {
                if (i > 0 && dp[i - 1][j] && s1.charAt(i - 1) == s3.charAt(i + j - 1)) dp[i][j] = true;
                if (j > 0 && dp[i][j - 1] && s2.charAt(j - 1) == s3.charAt(i + j - 1)) dp[i][j] = true;
            }
        return dp[n][m];
    }
}
```

