:::details 3. Bottom-up, one row (optimal space)
Row `i` only needs row `i − 1` (the old `dp[j]`) and the cell to its left (the new `dp[j − 1]`), so one array is enough.

**Java**

```java
class Solution {
    public boolean isInterleave(String s1, String s2, String s3) {
        int n = s1.length(), m = s2.length();
        if (n + m != s3.length()) return false;
        boolean[] dp = new boolean[m + 1];
        for (int i = 0; i <= n; i++)
            for (int j = 0; j <= m; j++) {
                if (i == 0 && j == 0) { dp[0] = true; continue; }
                boolean fromS1 = i > 0 && dp[j] && s1.charAt(i - 1) == s3.charAt(i + j - 1);         // old dp[j] = row above
                boolean fromS2 = j > 0 && dp[j - 1] && s2.charAt(j - 1) == s3.charAt(i + j - 1);     // new dp[j-1] = left
                dp[j] = fromS1 || fromS2;
            }
        return dp[m];
    }
}
```

