:::

:::details 2. Bottom-up 2-D table
`dp[i][j]` filled from the end: `dp[i][m] = 1`, and `dp[i][j] = dp[i+1][j] + (s[i] == t[j] ? dp[i+1][j+1] : 0)`.

**Java**

```java
class Solution {
    public int numDistinct(String s, String t) {
        int n = s.length(), m = t.length();
        int[][] dp = new int[n + 1][m + 1];
        for (int i = 0; i <= n; i++) dp[i][m] = 1;
        for (int i = n - 1; i >= 0; i--)
            for (int j = m - 1; j >= 0; j--) {
                dp[i][j] = dp[i + 1][j];
                if (s.charAt(i) == t.charAt(j)) dp[i][j] += dp[i + 1][j + 1];
            }
        return dp[0][0];
    }
}
```

