:::details 3. Bottom-up, one row (optimal space)
Keep `dp[j]` for the current `i`. Walking `j` **left to right**, `dp[j + 1]` still holds the previous row's value when `dp[j]` is updated, so the update can be done in place.

**Java**

```java
class Solution {
    public int numDistinct(String s, String t) {
        int m = t.length();
        int[] dp = new int[m + 1];
        dp[m] = 1;
        for (int i = s.length() - 1; i >= 0; i--)
            for (int j = 0; j < m; j++) // left to right: dp[j+1] is still last row's value
                if (s.charAt(i) == t.charAt(j)) dp[j] += dp[j + 1];
        return dp[0];
    }
}
```

**Python**

