**Pitfall:** Intermediate counts can exceed 32 bits even though the final answer fits. In Java, `int` addition wraps, but since the final answer fits, the wrapped arithmetic still ends on the right value. Python has big ints.

**Key idea:** Compare the last characters of the two prefixes. Equal → no cost, `d(i−1, j−1)`. Different → 1 + the best of delete `d(i−1, j)`, insert `d(i, j−1)`, replace `d(i−1, j−1)`.

```grid
