:::

:::details 3. Bottom-up, one row (optimal space)
Keep the previous row in one array. While walking a row, hold the old `dp[j−1]` (the diagonal) in a variable before overwriting it.

**Java**

```java
class Solution {
    public int minDistance(String word1, String word2) {
        int m = word2.length();
        int[] dp = new int[m + 1];
        for (int j = 0; j <= m; j++) dp[j] = j;
        for (int i = 1; i <= word1.length(); i++) {
            int diag = dp[0]; // old dp[i-1][j-1]
            dp[0] = i;
            for (int j = 1; j <= m; j++) {
                int above = dp[j];
                dp[j] = word1.charAt(i - 1) == word2.charAt(j - 1)
                    ? diag
                    : 1 + Math.min(diag, Math.min(above, dp[j - 1]));
                diag = above;
            }
        }
        return dp[m];
    }
}
```

