**Time:** O(n log n)
**Space:** O(1) besides the sort
:::

:::details 2. Sorted starts and ends separately
Sort all starts and all ends into two arrays. Meetings are clash-free exactly when, for every `i ≥ 1`, the `i`-th start is at or after the `(i−1)`-th end; otherwise two meetings are running at once.

**Java**

```java
class Solution {
    public boolean canAttendMeetings(int[][] intervals) {
        int n = intervals.length;
        int[] starts = new int[n], ends = new int[n];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) { starts[i] = intervals[i][0]; ends[i] = intervals[i][1]; }
        Arrays.sort(starts);
        Arrays.sort(ends);
        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++)
            if (starts[i] < ends[i - 1]) return false; // two meetings running at once
        return true;
    }
}
```

