:::details 3. Sweep line with a sorted map
Add `+1` at each start and `−1` at each end, in a sorted map. Walk the times in order keeping a running total; the max total is the answer. Ends and starts at the same time cancel inside one map entry, so back-to-back meetings share a room.

**Java**

```java
class Solution {
    public int minMeetingRooms(int[][] intervals) {
        TreeMap<Integer, Integer> delta = new TreeMap<>();
        for (int[] m : intervals) {
            delta.merge(m[0], 1, Integer::sum);
            delta.merge(m[1], -1, Integer::sum);
        }
        int running = 0, best = 0;
        for (int d : delta.values()) {
            running += d;
            best = Math.max(best, running);
        }
        return best;
    }
}
```

